              <td class="py-1 tabular-nums text-fg-2">
                {#if p.id === 'P3'}
                  {#each evals.image_spaces as s (s.model)}<div>{s.model}: HK agreement {fmt(s.hk_family)} → {s.hk_family !== null && s.hk_family >= evals.gates.reject_hk ? 'met' : 'not met'}</div>{/each}
                {:else if p.id === 'P4'}
                  <span class="text-muted">awaits the M4 triplets</span>
                {:else if scored.some((s) => s.hit)}
                  {#each scored as s (s.model)}{#if s.hit}<div>{s.model}: {fmt(s.hit.observed)} → {s.hit.met ? 'met' : 'NOT met'}</div>{/if}{/each}
                {:else}
                  <span class="text-muted">—</span>
                {/if}
              </td>
            </tr>
          {/each}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <h3 class="font-semibold">What was measured</h3>
    <div class="overflow-x-auto">
      <table class="w-full text-sm">
        <caption class="sr-only">Image spaces against the numeric default</caption>
        <thead class="text-left text-xs text-muted"><tr><th class="py-1 pr-3 font-medium">space</th><th class="py-1 pr-3 font-medium">C1 obs (gate ≥ {gate.c1})</th><th class="py-1 pr-3 font-medium">C5 obs (≥ {gate.c5})</th><th class="py-1 pr-3 font-medium">ρ vs Shape</th><th class="py-1 pr-3 font-medium">top-10 overlap with Shape</th><th class="py-1 pr-3 font-medium">HK class agreement</th><th class="py-1 font-medium">verdict</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {#each evals.image_spaces as s (s.model)}
            <tr class="border-t border-border tabular-nums">
              <td class="py-1 pr-3 font-mono text-xs">{s.model}{exposed?.model === s.model ? ' · exposed as “Visual”' : ''}</td>
              <td class="py-1 pr-3">{fmt(s.c1)} ✗</td>
              <td class="py-1 pr-3">{fmt(s.c5)} ✗</td>
              <td class="py-1 pr-3">{fmt(s.spearman_vs_blend, 2)}</td>
              <td class="py-1 pr-3">{fmtPctOf(s.top10_overlap)} same-year · {fmtPctOf(s.top10_overlap_anyyear)} any-year</td>
              <td class="py-1 pr-3">{fmt(s.hk_family)}</td>
              <td class="py-1">{s.verdict}{s.verdict !== s.expected_verdict ? ` (predicted ${s.expected_verdict})` : ''}</td>
            </tr>
          {/each}
          {#if blend}
            <tr class="border-t border-border tabular-nums text-fg-2"><td class="py-1 pr-3">Shape (for scale)</td><td class="py-1 pr-3">{fmt(blend.c1_obs)} ✓</td><td class="py-1 pr-3">{fmt(blend.c5_obs)} ✓</td><td class="py-1 pr-3">1</td><td class="py-1 pr-3">—</td><td class="py-1 pr-3">{fmt(g2Of('blend')?.hk_family)}</td><td class="py-1">{evals.verdicts.blend?.verdict}</td></tr>
          {/if}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>
      Read: the embeddings are <em>related</em> to shape (rank correlation {fmt(exposedSpace?.spearman_vs_blend, 2)} with
      Shape distance; class agreement above the {evals.gates.reject_hk} floor, so P3 held) but they are not continuous
      in time — a country's nearest picture is its own adjacent year only {fmt(visualRows[0]?.c1_obs, 2)}–{fmt(visualRows[visualRows.length - 1]?.c1_obs, 2)} of the
      time against a gate of {gate.c1}, and their top-10 lists share under a third of their members with Shape's. The
      invariance diagnostic explains why: recolouring the bars or adding a 2-px gap moves a render's embedding farther
      from itself than the nearest <em>different</em> pyramid sits, so these encoders separate rendering styles more
      than they separate populations. Both spaces were predicted to land at “{evals.prereg.expected_visual_verdict}” and
      landed one rung lower, at “{visualRows[0] ? evals.verdicts[visualRows[0].metric]?.verdict : '—'}”.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Why it ships anyway.</strong> By the owner's decision both methods are available: Shape is the default,
      and the image space with the better observed-span continuity ({exposed?.model}, rule: {exposed?.rule ?? 'better observed-span G1 C1'})
      is in the metric menu as “Visual”, labelled experimental, so anyone can see for themselves what a vision model
      thinks looks alike — and compare it with the numbers above. {#if exposed?.alternates?.length}The other space
      ({exposed.alternates.join(', ')}) is reachable by URL only.{/if} The human-triplet test (P4) has not run yet;
      if it ever favours Visual on notch-and-bulge anchors — the only claim the pre-registration permits — the record
      will say so here.
    </p>
  </section>

